    "maintenance-10": {
      "id": "maintenance-10",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The installed skill tells the coding agent when and how to use those tools. Installation places references/standards.md, references/components.md, references/components/<name>.md, and snapshot.json beside SKILL.md. These files are generated from the canonical corpus and manifests. They are not independent standards."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-11": {
      "id": "maintenance-11",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The catalog covers rich text, annotated Code, File Tree, Structured Table, State Shape, Interaction Surface, Canvas, Sequence, and Process Outline. One-line component purposes load with "
        },
        {
          "insert": "docs_begin",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": ". The full catalog and detailed references load only when needed. Connecting an MCP does not prove a client selected the skill. Test implicit use in each client."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-12": {
      "id": "maintenance-12",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Change Writing or Component Guidance"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-13": {
      "id": "maintenance-13",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "1. For wording and standards, read the canonical document through Docs tools, apply a typed edit, and run "
        },
        {
          "insert": "docs_check",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " with the task ID. When a style guide edit changes a rule the digest summarizes, update "
        },
        {
          "insert": "STYLE_DIGEST",
          "attributes": {
            "code": true
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " to match. For tool-use workflow, edit the source SKILL.md. Project-specific standards overrides are not implemented."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-14": {
      "id": "maintenance-14",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "2. For component selection, update the component manifest authoring metadata and its canonical reference together. Change the shared visual guidance only when the selection rule itself changes."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-15": {
      "id": "maintenance-15",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "3. For a new component, register its bundle, state schema, typed actions, and rendering using the existing component contract. Add its canonical documentation and manifest metadata. A skill reference alone does not implement editing tools."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-16": {
      "id": "maintenance-16",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "4. Refresh the client installation and begin a new authoring task. Restart the service first when imported TypeScript changed. Inspect docs_guidance for the changed component and verify a real typed edit."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-17": {
      "id": "maintenance-17",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Synchronization and Updates",
          "attributes": {
            "reference": {
              "kind": "doc",
              "path": "40-guides/10-docs-mcp/30-sync"
            }
          }
        },
        {
          "insert": " gives the commands and restart decisions."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-18": {
      "id": "maintenance-18",
      "type": "heading",
      "props": {
        "level": 2
      },
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "Built-in Agents and PromptKit"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-19": {
      "id": "maintenance-19",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "The Docs Lab context loader at packages/docs-kernel/catalog/docs-lab-editor/context/index.ts and the sibling agent-kernel/catalog/docs-writer/context/index.ts both use the shared authoring-guidance renderer. Their prompts, model configuration, context loading, and staged editing sessions remain owned by those agents. External MCP edits do not run those agents."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    "maintenance-20": {
      "id": "maintenance-20",
      "type": "paragraph",
      "props": {},
      "text": [
        {
          "insert": "PromptKit remains responsible for its own prompt machinery. This integration has no PromptKit editing adapter and does not turn every internal prompt into an MCP prompt. A future product service can follow the same separation between typed operations, maintained knowledge, and client installation. Such adapters must document their own state ownership and validation before claiming coverage."
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  }
